# Kept in git, not shipped to Vercel.
#
# Every pattern below is ANCHORED with a leading slash so it matches only the repository
# root. Unanchored, a bare `compliance/` also matches `website/src/components/compliance/`,
# which is exactly what happened on 2026-11-05: a new component folder of that name was
# silently stripped from the deploy and the build died on
# "Could not resolve ../components/compliance/TriggerDisclaimers.astro".
# If you add a pattern here, anchor it.

/brand/
/Guidelines/
/seo-aeo-dtc-research/
/presentations/
/email-campaigns/
/compliance/
/blog articles/
/scripts/

# Full-resolution source headshots. scripts/import-headshots.mjs turns these into the
# optimized website/public/team/{slug}.{avif,webp,jpg} files that pages actually use, and
# that script runs locally, never on Vercel. Everything under website/public/ is published
# verbatim, so leaving these in the deploy pushed 24MB of unreferenced full-res staff photos
# to the public internet on every build. Kept in git (the team edits them); just not shipped.
/website/public/images/headshots/
